#: Game.Levels.TylerWorld.L02_provingimplications2
msgid "Lean obviously knows that §0, so the theorem is proved.\n"
"\n"
"**Warning:** Ending up at §1 here is only fine because §2 applies a logical equivalence (or equality). Applying one-directional implications works differently, as we will see in the next level."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `Not_or`
#. §1: `Or_and_left`
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L04_equiv
msgid "### **Level 4**\n"
"This logical equivalence is sometimes called **Proof by cases**. We'll use this a lot in the future. It basically tells us how to approach proofs where we have a hypothesis in the form a disjunction. We'll need two new laws of logic to pass this level. 🔍 Check out the entries for §0 and §1."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L06_equiv
msgid "### **🤔 Level 6?**"
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.TylerWorld.L03_modusponens
msgid "This last message appears if the level is solved."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P → Q`
