#: Game.Levels.TylerWorld.L02_provingimplications2
msgid "Proving statements of the form §0"
msgstr ""

#. §0: ```
#. (H₁ ∧ H₂) → P
#. ```
#. §1: ```
#. H₁ → (H₂ → P)
#. ```
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L03_equiv
msgid "## **Level 3**\n"
"Oftentimes, we'll have implications of the form\n"
"§0\n"
"For programmatic purposes, this kind of proposition is better expressed in the following way:\n"
"§1\n"
"This exercise demonstrates that this process of translating the first form into the second (called **currying**) is logically valid."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `h`
#. §1: `exact h`
#: Game.Levels.TylerWorld.L01_provingimplications_alt
msgid "We now have to observe that we've proven what has been asked of us. §0 is now the goal, so by writing §1, we tell Lean that we've established the goal."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L02_equiv
msgid "An implication is logically equivalent to its contrapositive."
msgstr ""

