#. §0: `x = x`
#. §1: `P ↔ P`
#. §2: `x ~ x`
#. §3: `∼`
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L01_equiv
msgid "This tactic clears a goal whose target has the form §0 or §1 (or §2 where §3 is any relation that has a reflexivity lemma tagged with the attribute @[refl] -- we'll talk more about relations later)."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P → Q`
#. §1: `P → Q`
#. §2: `P`
#. §3: `Q`
#. §4: `intro`
#. §5: `P`
#: Game.Levels.TylerWorld.L01_provingimplications_alt
msgid "The most fundamental proof technique is how to directly address goals of the form §0. To prove §1, we can assume §2 and try to deduce §3.\n"
"\n"
"The §4 tactic lets us assume §5 in this case."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `P → Q`
#. §1: `Q → P`
#. §2: `intro`
#. §3: `P`
#: Game.Levels.TylerWorld.L02_provingimplications2
msgid "When proving statements of the form §0 where it is not true that §1, proofs necessarily look a bit different than the previous problem.\n"
"\n"
"The §2 tactic lets us assume §3 in this case."
msgstr ""

#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L03_equiv
msgid "Doc on currying"
msgstr ""

#. §0: `rewrite[e]`
#. §1: `e`
#. §2: `e`
#. §3: `←`
#. §4: `<-`
#. §5: `e : a = b`
#. §6: `rewrite[e]`
#. §7: `a`
#. §8: `b`
#. §9: `rewrite[← e]`
#. §10: `b`
#. §11: `a`
#. §12: `e₁`
#. §13: `e₂`
#. §14: `eₙ`
#. §15: ```
#. rewrite [e₁, ..., eₙ]
#. ```
#. §16: `rewrite [e] at l`
#. §17: `e`
#. §18: `l`
#. §19: `l`
#. §20: `⊢`
#. §21: `|-`
#. §22: `←`
#. §23: `\\left`
#. §24: `⊢`
#. §25: `\\vdash`
#: Game.Levels.EquivWorld.L01_equiv
msgid "The tactic §0 applies the identity/equivalence §1 as a **rewrite** rule to the target.\n"
"\n"
"If §2 is preceded by left arrow (§3 or §4), the rewrite is applied in the reverse direction. For example, if §5 then ...\n"
"* §6 replaces all instances of §7 with §8 in the target\n"
"* §9 replaces all instances of §10 with §11 in the target\n"
"\n"
"If §12,§13,...,§14 is a sequence of identities then\n"
"§15\n"
"applies the given rules sequentially.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, §16 rewrites §17 at location(s) §18, where §19 is a list of hypotheses in the local context or the main goal §20 (or §21).\n"
"\n"
"### **⌨ Typesetting tip**\n"
"To pretty print the left-arrow §22 use §23. To pretty print the symbol §24 use §25."
msgstr ""

